 ## Verification
 
-The package test owns every statement, branch, and function in the bridge implementation. It covers durable one-time reminders, text-only replay, current-session and cross-session authorization, request construction, literal/credential/environment key resolution, structured and malformed visual responses, limits, duplicate ids, cancellation, HTTP and JSON failures, redacted results, configuration rejection, contribution disposal, and reject/enter pre-step chaining. ACP content and API-proxy tests cover the shared image admission and model capability paths. A deployment test must also list the configured visual model through the gateway and complete one real image inspection before the overlay is promoted.
+The package test owns every statement, branch, line, and function in the bridge implementation. It covers durable one-time reminders, text-only replay, current-session and cross-session authorization, request construction, literal/credential/environment key resolution, structured and malformed visual responses, limits, duplicate ids, cancellation, HTTP and JSON failures, redacted results, configuration rejection, contribution disposal, reject/enter pre-step chaining, keyed browser registration and teardown, visual lifecycle states, and the shared elapsed-time presentation. ACP content and API-proxy tests cover the shared image admission and model capability paths. A deployment test must also list the configured visual model through the gateway, complete one real image inspection, and capture its running and settled visual rows before the overlay is promoted.
 
 ## Consequences
 
diff --git a/.agents/notes/implemented/feature/2026-08-22-text-model-vision-subagent-bridge.zh.md b/.agents/notes/implemented/feature/2026-08-22-text-model-vision-subagent-bridge.zh.md
